from pathlib import Path
from runpy import run_path
g=run_path(str(Path(__file__).with_name('author-tools-generator.py')))
L=g['lesson']; C=g['course']
def J(*a): return L(*a,language='javascript')

C('clean-code','Clean code is code that people can read and change with confidence. We will improve small JavaScript examples by naming things clearly, keeping jobs small and making assumptions visible.','Run these JavaScript examples here. Readability is a team choice, so use the project\'s existing style when you work with others.','https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/MDN/Writing_guidelines/Code_style_guide/JavaScript',[
J('Write for the next reader','Code is read many times. A clear name explains the purpose of a value without making the reader solve a puzzle.','const numberOfBooks = 4;\nconsole.log(numberOfBooks);','The result is 4. The name tells us what is being counted.','Compare numberOfBooks with a name like x.','A very short name is not always easier to understand.','Which name explains the value better?','numberOfBooks','x'),
J('Name actions with verbs','Function names should explain what the action does. A reader should not need to inspect every line to understand a call.','function addPrices(first, second) { return first + second; }\nconsole.log(addPrices(3, 4));','The result is 7. The function name says it adds prices.','Name a function that removes a saved book.','Avoid names such as doStuff that hide the purpose.','Which function name is clearer?','addPrices','processThing'),
J('Keep one job in a function','A small function with one clear job is easier to test and reuse. Separate a calculation from drawing a page.','const totalPrice = prices => prices.reduce((sum, price) => sum + price, 0);\nconsole.log(totalPrice([2, 3]));','The result is 5. This function calculates a total and does not change the page.','Write a separate function that formats the total as text.','Do not mix a simple calculation with unrelated saving and navigation.','What is this function\'s job?','Calculate a total','Send an email'),
J('Replace unexplained numbers','A named constant explains why a special value appears. It also gives the rule one clear place to change.','const MAX_BOOKS = 3;\nconst canBorrow = count => count < MAX_BOOKS;\nconsole.log(canBorrow(2));','The result is true. The name explains why 3 is used in the rule.','Change the limit to 4 and test count 3.','Do not name every obvious arithmetic value; name values whose meaning needs explaining.','What does MAX_BOOKS explain?','The borrowing limit','The current number borrowed'),
J('Return early for simple cases','A guard clause handles a special case early. It can reduce deep nesting and make the main path easier to follow.','function greet(name) {\n  if (!name) return "Hello!";\n  return "Hi " + name;\n}\nconsole.log(greet(""));','The result is Hello!. The empty-name case ends before the normal greeting.','Call greet with Asha.','Make sure an early return does not skip work that must always happen.','Which case returns early?','An empty name','Every non-empty name'),
J('Avoid needless repeated rules','When the same rule appears in several places, changes can be missed. Put a shared rule in one clear function.','const passes = score => score >= 5;\nconsole.log(passes(4), passes(7));','The output is false true. Both checks use the same passing rule.','Add a third call without copying the rule.','Two similar lines do not always represent the same rule; do not combine unrelated ideas.','Why share this function?','To keep one passing rule','To hide every variable'),
J('Comments explain reasons','A useful comment explains why a choice was made. The code should already explain ordinary steps through names.','// Zero gives an empty basket a useful total.\nconst total = [].reduce((sum, price) => sum + price, 0);\nconsole.log(total);','The result is 0. The comment explains why a starting value is present.','Write a comment explaining a unusual business limit.','Update comments when the code changes; a wrong comment misleads readers.','What should a useful comment explain?','The reason for a choice','Only repeat the next word of code'),
J('Make errors helpful','An error should say what input was wrong or what action failed. It should not expose private details.','function setAge(age) {\n  if (!Number.isInteger(age) || age < 0) throw new Error("Age must be a whole number of zero or more");\n  return age;\n}\nconsole.log(setAge(10));','The result is 10. Invalid ages would get a message that explains the rule.','Try a decimal age and read the error.','Do not print secret values in error messages.','Which message helps a caller fix the input?','Age must be a whole number of zero or more','Something happened'),
J('Prefer clear conditions','A condition is easier to read when it states one clear question. Name a complicated condition if its purpose is not obvious.','const isOpen = true;\nconst hasSpace = false;\nconst canJoin = isOpen && hasSpace;\nconsole.log(canJoin);','The result is false because both conditions must be true.','Set hasSpace to true.','Be careful with double negatives such as notNotReady.','What must be true to join?','Open and has space','Only open'),
J('Avoid surprising changes','A function that returns a new value can be easier to reason about than one that changes its input. Make changes clear in the function name or contract.','const original = [3, 1, 2];\nconst sorted = [...original].sort((a, b) => a - b);\nconsole.log(original.join(","));\nconsole.log(sorted.join(","));','The original stays 3,1,2; the copy becomes 1,2,3.','Use another list and compare both outputs.','sort changes its array, so copy first when the caller expects the original to stay.','Why make a copy before sort?','To preserve the original list','To change its numbers randomly'),
J('Refactor without changing behaviour','Refactoring improves the code structure while keeping the same intended behaviour. Tests help check that the behaviour stayed the same.','const before = n => n * 2 + 1;\nfunction after(n) { const doubled = n * 2; return doubled + 1; }\nconsole.log(before(3) === after(3));','The result is true for this input. More useful cases would strengthen the check.','Compare both functions for zero and a negative number.','Do not mix a large behaviour change with a readability-only change unless the scope is clear.','What should refactoring preserve?','Intended behaviour','Every old variable name'),
J('Review a small change','A focused review checks whether a change solves its stated problem and keeps the code readable. Small changes are easier to inspect.','const trimTitle = title => title.trim();\nconsole.log(trimTitle("  Moon  ") === "Moon");','The check passes. The change has one purpose: removing spaces at the ends.','Add a check showing spaces inside a title are preserved.','Avoid unrelated rewrites while fixing one small issue.','What is the stated purpose of trimTitle?','Remove outer spaces','Remove every space'),
])

C('cybersecurity','Cybersecurity protects information and systems from misuse and mistakes. This course teaches everyday defensive habits through fictional school examples and safe local demonstrations.','Use only your own practice data. These lessons do not teach attacks against other people\'s systems and do not require a real account or secret.','https://www.cisa.gov/secure-our-world',[
L('Protect information','Security includes keeping information private, correct and available when needed. These three goals are often called confidentiality, integrity and availability.','Private: only the teacher sees a private note\nCorrect: a score is not changed by accident\nAvailable: the lesson page opens when needed','Each line protects a different part of using information safely.','Give one example of each goal for a school library.','Protecting privacy alone does not guarantee a service remains usable or correct.','Which goal protects information from unwanted changes?','Integrity','Availability'),
L('Think about the thing you protect','An asset is something valuable, such as a file or saved work. A threat is something that might harm it. A risk considers how likely and harmful that problem is.','Asset: a class project file\nThreat: accidental deletion\nControl: a tested backup copy','The backup reduces the harm from losing the working file.','Name a threat to a shared classroom tablet and one useful protection.','Do not start with a tool before naming the problem it should reduce.','What is the asset in this example?','The project file','The word backup'),
L('Use strong unique passwords','A unique password is used for only one account. A password manager can create and remember long passwords so one leak does not unlock many accounts.','Account A: its own long password\nAccount B: a different long password\nPassword manager: stores them in its protected vault','Reusing one password would connect the risk of both accounts. Never put real passwords into this tutorial.','Explain why a different password for each account helps.','A password written as an example in public is not a password to use.','Why avoid password reuse?','One leak should not unlock other accounts','It makes typing shorter'),
L('Add another sign-in factor','Multi-factor authentication asks for more than one kind of proof. A security key or an authenticator can add protection beyond a password.','Something you know: password\nSomething you have: security key\nTwo factors protect one sign-in','Two passwords are still both things you know. Different kinds of proof are what make multiple factors.','Identify the factor type of a physical security key.','Never share a one-time code with someone who contacts you unexpectedly.','Which pair uses different factor types?','Password and security key','Two passwords'),
L('Spot suspicious messages','Phishing is a trick that tries to make someone reveal information or take a harmful action. Pause when a message pressures you to act quickly.','Message: Your school files vanish in 5 minutes! Send your password now.\nSafer response: do not reply; contact the school through a known channel.','The urgent threat and request for a password are warning signs.','Write a calm response plan for a suspicious message without replying to its sender.','A familiar logo or display name does not prove who sent a message.','What is the safer next step?','Check through a known trusted channel','Send the password quickly'),
L('Check the actual address','A link label can differ from its destination. Read the real host name carefully before entering private information.','Label shown: School portal\nActual host: school.example.attacker.test\nDomain controlled here: attacker.test','The word school appears in a subdomain; it does not make the destination the school\'s site. This is a fictional address.','Compare that address with portal.school.test.','A padlock means an encrypted connection, not that the website is honest.','Who controls the example host?','The owner of attacker.test','Automatically the school'),
L('Keep software updated','Updates often fix known weaknesses as well as ordinary bugs. Install them through the software\'s trusted update route.','Known issue discovered\nMaker publishes a fix\nYou update and restart when required','Using the fixed version reduces exposure to that known issue.','Find where a browser shows its update status without downloading random tools.','Do not install an update from an unexpected message attachment.','Where should an update come from?','The trusted maker or built-in updater','Any message claiming urgent update'),
L('Give only needed access','Least privilege means giving each person or program only the access needed for its job. This limits damage from mistakes or misuse.','Reader: can view lesson files\nEditor: can change lesson text\nPublisher: can release a reviewed version','The jobs have different permissions. A reader does not need the power to publish.','Choose permissions for someone who only checks spelling.','Do not give administrator access merely because it is easier to set up.','What access does a reader need?','View lesson files','Publish and delete everything'),
J('Treat text as text','User-supplied text should not become executable page code by accident. textContent places text into a page without treating it as HTML.','const message = document.createElement("p");\nmessage.textContent = "<b>Hello</b>";\nconsole.log(message.textContent);','The console prints the literal text <b>Hello</b>. It is not turned into a bold element by textContent.','Use another string containing angle brackets.','Do not put untrusted text into innerHTML. Choose a safe text API when you need text.','Which API keeps this input as plain text?','textContent','innerHTML'),
L('Validate at a trusted boundary','Validation checks that data follows a rule. Browser checks help the user, but a real backend must check received data too because browser code can be changed.','Page rule: quantity must be a whole number from 1 to 5\nBackend rule in a real service: check the same limits before saving\nThis tutorial app: has no backend or accounts','The page is useful guidance, not a trusted security barrier for another service.','List valid quantities and one invalid quantity for the rule.','Do not trust a value just because a browser form accepted it.','Can a real service rely only on browser validation?','No','Yes'),
L('Back up and practise recovery','A backup is another copy of important data. A useful backup must be readable and restorable, not merely present.','Working file: project.txt\nBackup copy: stored separately\nRecovery practice: open a copy and check the contents','The practice checks whether the saved copy can actually help after loss.','Describe how to test a backup without deleting the original.','A copy on the same failing disk may be lost with the original.','What should you test about a backup?','That you can recover useful data','Only that its name exists'),
L('Respond calmly to a problem','An incident is an event that may harm security. Stop risky actions, preserve useful facts and get help from the responsible person.','Unexpected sign-in notice\n1. Do not follow the message link\n2. Open the service through a known address\n3. Review activity and contact its support if needed','The steps avoid adding a new risk while checking the warning. A young learner should ask a trusted adult for help.','Write down the time and what you observed without sharing secret codes.','Do not erase useful evidence or accuse someone before the facts are checked.','What is a useful first response?','Pause and use a known trusted route','Click every link to investigate'),
])
